\pard\s1\f0\fs40\b\sa200\keepn SellerShield AI member 3 complete guide\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Backend and rules engine from product idea to working demo\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Prepared for the backend owner on 7 November 2026\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 You build the server that connects payment records, customer messages, shipping labels and the merchant dashboard. Your code compares addresses, applies explicit rules, stores the evidence behind each result and returns a decision the merchant can understand. Your first milestone is a stored order that produces an explained BLOCKED result through the API.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Read sections 1 to 5 to understand the product and your tools. Follow sections 6 to 13 while working on the backend. Sections 14 to 20 cover testing, teammate integration, planned extensions, deployment and the demo. The appendices provide a glossary, troubleshooting steps and references.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The project documents define the team responsibilities. The implementation described here is the single-merchant sandbox backend in the Sentrix workspace. Features marked planned need further work before the team can demonstrate them as working integrations.\par
\pard\s2\f0\fs30\b\sb260\sa130\keepn 1 The product in plain language\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 A customer pays through PayPal using shipping address A. Later, they ask support to ship to address B. A seller might accept the request without checking how it affects the original payment transaction. SellerShield compares the payment address with the intended shipment destination before dispatch.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 For example, the payment says 123 Main Street, Apartment 4, Austin, Texas 78701. The shipping label says 987 Main Street at the same city and ZIP code. SellerShield identifies the changed house number and tells the merchant to hold dispatch.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The product has a practical purpose even when the customer made an honest mistake. An address-change request is not proof of fraud. Your system detects a destination mismatch or uncertainty and helps the merchant review it.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 PayPal's US Seller Protection policy requires shipment to the shipping address on the transaction details page, along with other conditions. Address alignment is one check, not a guarantee that a future dispute will be decided in the seller's favor. The dashboard's PROTECTED label is SellerShield's local rule result. See reference 3 for the policy.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The intended merchant experience is to see a queue of orders, open an order, compare the addresses, read the reasons, then choose an action. Later features help prepare dispute evidence and perform merchant-approved PayPal actions.\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn What the three results mean\b0\par
