\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Before a label exists, a message can set MESSAGE_FLAGGED when it requests an address change. The current backend does not compare the proposed message address to decide dispatch. Final address evaluation uses the PayPal shipping address and the latest parsed label. Message intent confidence can still cause REVIEW after a label exists.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The order of arrival can vary. A label can arrive before a message. A message can first arrive without analysis and receive analysis later. When the latest relevant inputs change, the service recomputes the result and preserves a new verdict snapshot.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Three different addresses have three different meanings. The PayPal address is the original transaction reference. The proposed address is what the customer requested in a message. The label address is where the shipment is intended to go. Keep these separate in names, storage and explanations.\par
