\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 FastAPI handles requests. Uvicorn runs the server process. Pydantic checks payload shapes. SQLAlchemy reads and writes records. Postgres stores those records. Alembic creates or changes the tables. These are different jobs within the same backend.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 usaddress identifies components probabilistically. It cannot confirm that an address exists and does not normalize it for you. Your code adds suffix and direction mappings, preserves important components and routes unsupported or ambiguous cases to REVIEW. RapidFuzz provides string similarity, not a shipping authorization.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The current project already has SQLAlchemy and Alembic. Keep those choices rather than introducing SQLModel or another database layer. No queue, Redis service, vector database or separate model-training pipeline is needed for the current slice.\par
