\pard\s0\fs8\sa60\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Keep changes in the layer that owns the behavior. Change field constraints in schemas, comparison policy in rules, cross-record workflows in service, HTTP handling in main and schema changes in migrations. A rule change should not require copying comparison logic into routes or the frontend.\par
\pard\s2\f0\fs30\b\sb260\sa130\keepn 7 Set up and run locally\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Use Python 3.12, Docker Desktop and a terminal in the project root. The following commands are for PowerShell. Read the commands before running them; they install dependencies, start a local database and insert synthetic demo orders.\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn Create the Python environment\b0\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn Set-Location 'C:\\Users\\Hp\\Documents\\Sentrix'\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn py -3.12 -m venv .venv\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn .\\.venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn python --version\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep python -m pip install -r requirements.txt\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 If the py launcher is unavailable, use the path to a Python 3.12 executable. A different system Python does not establish compatibility with the project's 3.12 target. If PowerShell blocks activation, call .\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe and other executables by their full environment paths instead of changing machine-wide policy.\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn Start the database and set configuration\b0\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn docker compose up -d --wait\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn $env:DATABASE_URL = 'postgresql+psycopg://sellershield:local-only@localhost:5432/sellershield'\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn $env:MERCHANT_USERNAME = 'merchant'\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn $env:MERCHANT_PASSWORD = 'replace-with-your-own-long-random-demo-password'\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn $env:CORS_ORIGINS = 'http://localhost:5173'\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn alembic upgrade head\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn python -m app.seed\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --no-access-log\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The database password local-only is the local Docker example value, not a credential to reuse on a hosted database. Choose a private merchant password. Avoid placing credentials in screenshots, committed files or a public frontend build.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The app reads process environment variables. Copying .env.example to .env does not load it automatically. Set variables in the shell that starts the app or configure the host's environment settings.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Docker Compose binds Postgres to the local machine and uses a named volume. Stopping containers normally preserves that volume. Avoid commands that remove volumes unless you intend to discard the local database.\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn Confirm the backend is reachable\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Open http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs in a browser. Authorize with the configured merchant username and password. GET /health/ready should return a ready response. GET /orders requires authentication and should show the seeded scenarios.\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep Invoke-RestMethod 'http://127.0.0.1:8000/health/ready'\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The health endpoint checks database connectivity. It does not verify the full application schema, PayPal connectivity or AI availability. Run migrations before treating the service as usable.\par
\pard\s2\f0\fs30\b\sb260\sa130\keepn 8 Understand the shared contracts\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 app/schemas.py is the source of truth for requests and responses. The base contract rejects unknown fields. A typo such as confidence_score in place of confidence should fail validation rather than silently disappear.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The current address schema supports country US. Amounts use USD and positive decimal strings with two fractional digits. State format and ZIP validity are checked during address normalization. Some address fields accept empty strings at the schema level so incomplete data can be preserved and routed to REVIEW.\par
