\pard\s0\fs8\sa60\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The full ZIP extension is preserved. A five-digit ZIP and the same ZIP with a four-digit extension are not automatically treated as equivalent by the current code. Missing unit information on one address versus a present unit on the other currently produces a unit difference; with otherwise reliable inputs it can produce BLOCKED. These are current behaviors to discuss with evaluated fixtures before changing policy.\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn Verdict applies uncertainty before mismatch\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The current precedence is explicit:\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn Any configured uncertainty -> REVIEW\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn Otherwise MISMATCH         -> BLOCKED\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep Otherwise                  -> PROTECTED\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Uncertainty includes incomplete or unsupported addresses, missing label confidence, label confidence below 0.90, intent confidence below 0.90, AMBIGUOUS intent or a seller-protection status other than ELIGIBLE. A confidence of exactly 0.90 meets the current threshold.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 PARTIALLY_ELIGIBLE and UNKNOWN both route to REVIEW in this implementation. They do not automatically pass. This is the configured local policy, not a statement that every partially eligible PayPal transaction lacks all protection.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 A street or city difference with a RapidFuzz ratio of at least 85 also causes REVIEW. The code treats similar wording as a reason for human judgment, not proof of equivalence. These numeric cutoffs are local heuristics that need evaluation on fixtures.\par
