\pard\s0\fs8\sa60\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Capture IDs are unique. Message external IDs are unique within an order. Labels and verdicts append as new records. The API has no route to edit a saved verdict snapshot, although database administrators can still change stored data. An application audit table is not cryptographic tamper-proof storage.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Amounts are stored as decimal numeric values and returned as two-decimal strings. Keep currency with the amount. Avoid binary floating point when handling payments.\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn Transactions keep related changes together\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The request-scoped database dependency begins a transaction. A successful operation commits when the transaction exits. An exception rolls it back. A label insert, verdict insert and order-state update should succeed together or leave no partial update.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 flush sends pending changes to the database inside the current transaction. commit makes the transaction durable. The shared ingest_capture helper flushes but leaves the commit to its caller. Member 1 must call it inside an appropriate transaction.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Message and label routes lock the order row before modifying inputs. On Postgres, this serializes concurrent changes to the same order so two requests do not compute results from inconsistent input sets. SQLite tests do not establish that the Postgres row-locking path works.\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn Latest inputs and the current view\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 latest selects the record with the greatest internal ID for the requested order. view assembles the order and latest message, label and verdict. recompute updates timestamps, handles the no-label state and otherwise evaluates the latest inputs before appending a verdict.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 This is a simple latest-message policy. A newer unrelated message can become the message used in the current view. If the product must retain every unresolved address-change request, extend this behavior deliberately and test message ordering; do not assume the prototype already does that.\par
