\pard\s0\fs8\sa60\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Additional useful cases include missing units, ZIP extensions, multiple messages, out-of-order analysis, multiple labels and disconnects during external actions. Add tests when implementing those behaviors or resolving their policy. Do not claim they are covered by a neighboring test.\par
\pard\s2\f0\fs30\b\sb260\sa130\keepn 15 Integrating Member 1 and Member 2\b0\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn Member 1 supplies trusted capture records\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Member 1 should verify the PayPal webhook signature, fetch trusted order or capture information, map it to Capture and call ingest_capture. The helper must not be exposed through an unauthenticated public route that accepts a claimed PayPal address.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The existing integration shape is:\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn from app.db import session_factory\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn from app.schemas import Capture\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn from app.service import ingest_capture\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn \par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn sessions = session_factory()\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn \par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn with sessions.begin() as db:\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn     capture = Capture.model_validate(normalized_record)\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep     order = ingest_capture(db, capture)\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 normalized_record must come from Member 1's verified workflow. Identical capture retries return the existing order. Conflicting capture data or identifiers raise Conflict. The caller owns the transaction commit.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 If the verified webhook router is mounted inside this FastAPI app, it should use PayPal's verification process rather than the merchant Basic-auth dependency. Agree on error mapping and webhook acknowledgement behavior with Member 1.\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn Member 2 supplies extracted facts\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Give Member 2 the schemas and exact examples. They should return supported intent values, a source quote, a confidence within 0 to 1 and an optional proposed US address. The label parser should return the complete destination components, tracking number, carrier and confidence when available.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Agree whether Member 2 calls internal functions, mounts a router or submits to the existing protected intake routes. The current backend accepts analysis; it does not invoke an LLM or a vision model itself. Describe the adapter explicitly so neither teammate waits for the other to implement it.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 If extraction fails, preserve an understandable failure and hold for review. Do not manufacture a plausible address or a high confidence just to make the contract pass. Customer text and label content are untrusted input, including instructions embedded within them.\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn Your handoff to Member 4\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Provide the API base URL, /docs location, successful and failing payloads, null-result behavior, source marker and error statuses. Explain that /labels takes parsed JSON, not multipart image data. Agree where the image-upload UI will call Member 2's implementation.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The frontend should display backend verdicts and reasons. It should not recompute policy in JavaScript. Use runtime credentials for the single-merchant demo and avoid committing them or embedding a shared password into a public build.\par
\pard\s2\f0\fs30\b\sb260\sa130\keepn 16 Planned merchant actions and evidence\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 This section explains later work from the architecture plan. These capabilities are not implemented by the current routes.\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn Refunds tracking and replacement orders\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Your role is to validate the merchant request, check order state, coordinate Member 1's integration and record the result. Member 1 implements PayPal calls and protocol details. Add an action record and clear states when this work begins; the existing four tables do not represent a complete financial-action history.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 For an action, authorize the merchant on the server, identify the exact order and current inputs, record the request and pass a stable retry identifier to the integration where supported. Only record success after a confirmed successful result. A timeout can mean outcome unknown; reconcile it before repeating a financial operation.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Creating a reorder link is different from receiving a paid replacement order. Entering tracking is different from PayPal accepting tracking. A local BLOCKED result is different from a refund. Show these states separately.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Human review also needs a designed API. The expanded state diagram allows review decisions, but the current implementation has no merchant override route or approval record. Store who approved what, when and against which input version before describing that feature as complete.\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn Evidence preparation and submission\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Build a stable snapshot of original transaction data, relevant customer messages, label information, comparisons, verdicts, action history and available tracking facts. Member 2 can draft a summary from those stored facts. Avoid adding claims that are absent from the records.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Serialize the saved bundle deterministically and compute SHA-256 over its exact bytes using hashlib. Retain the same bytes or a durable version identifier for later checking. A hash detects a change relative to that saved value; it does not authenticate the original transaction or stop someone from replacing both bundle and hash.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Separate preview from submission. Record merchant approval for the exact evidence version. If the pack changes, require review of the changed pack. Member 1 handles the provide-evidence request and response. Mark EVIDENCE_SUBMITTED only after the submission is confirmed, not merely after pack generation.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 A boolean approved supplied by the browser is insufficient by itself. The backend must authenticate the merchant, check authority over the order and bind approval to the actual action and version.\par
\pard\s2\f0\fs30\b\sb260\sa130\keepn 17 Deploying the backend\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 render.yaml defines a Python web service and a managed Postgres database in the same region. The checked-in configuration selects paid service plans. Review the host's displayed resources and charges before creating them. Having a YAML file does not mean those resources are already deployed.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Use the Git repository and branch agreed by the team. If the workspace is only a folder, create or connect the intended repository before configuring the host. Avoid assuming a remote exists because source files are present.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The deployment sequence is dependency installation, database migration, then application startup. The configured start command binds to the host-provided PORT on all interfaces and disables access logging.\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn Build       pip install -r requirements.txt\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn Pre deploy  alembic upgrade head\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep\keepn Start       uvicorn app.main:app --host 0.0.0.0\par
\pard\s0\f1\fs18\li120\sa0\sl220\slmult0\keep             --port $PORT --no-access-log --log-level info\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 The displayed start command wraps for readability; render.yaml contains it on one line.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Set MERCHANT_USERNAME, MERCHANT_PASSWORD and the actual frontend CORS_ORIGINS in the hosting configuration. The blueprint injects the database connection string. Do not put live secrets into source control or use the local-only database password remotely.\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn Deployment checks\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 1. Confirm dependency installation and migration complete successfully.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 2. Call /health/ready and confirm the service reaches Postgres.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 3. Request /orders without credentials and expect 401.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 4. Authenticate and check queue and detail responses.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 5. Insert only synthetic scenarios for the demo when desired.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 6. Run the frontend against the deployed backend and verify CORS and auth.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 7. Recreate or restart the app and confirm stored order data remains.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 8. Exercise one message and label flow and inspect the saved verdict.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Postgres preserves structured records independently of the web process. If image upload is added later, local web-service files are not automatically durable. Choose a persistent file-storage location and store its reference in the database.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Keep production or real customer data outside the public hackathon demo. The current app has one merchant credential pair and no tenant isolation, account lifecycle or production payment workflow.\par
\pard\s2\f0\fs30\b\sb260\sa130\keepn 18 The demo you should make reliable\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Your backend demo should prove that an input reaches the rules, an explained verdict reaches the frontend and the database retains the decision. The current seeded version can demonstrate all three local verdicts. A real PayPal sandbox demonstration additionally needs Member 1's verified integration.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Start with DEMO-CLEAN and show the original address, matching label and PROTECTED result. Then open DEMO-MISMATCH and show the changed house number and BLOCKED reason. Finally, open DEMO-UNCERTAIN and show why the lower confidence requires REVIEW.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 For a live walkthrough, send a new message and parsed label through the intake routes, refresh the dashboard and show the new result. Identify the message source and parsed label as simulated until the corresponding integrations run. Avoid calling a fixture capture a PayPal response.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Keep a known fixture set and a separate demo database. Prepare endpoint examples in advance, confirm credentials privately and rehearse with the actual deployed frontend. Do not install dependencies or change the schema during the recording.\par
\pard\s3\f0\fs24\b\sb180\sa100\keepn Definition of done for your current slice\b0\par
