\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 At each check-in, report the working outcome, the next integration you need and one concrete blocker if there is one. For example, say that parsed-label evaluation works but no image adapter is connected, rather than saying that the AI flow is done.\par
\pard\s2\f0\fs30\b\sb260\sa130\keepn 20 Common mistakes to catch before handoff\b0\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Do not overwrite paypal_address with the proposed address. That destroys the reference needed for comparison. Keep a replacement order as a separately identified transaction.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Do not interpret a high fuzzy score as destination equality. House numbers, units and directional components need explicit attention. A single character can identify a different apartment or street.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Do not treat REVIEW as a minor warning that permits automatic dispatch. It is the path for uncertainty and unconfirmed eligibility. Frontend actions should reflect that workflow.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Do not describe the current backend as reading images or calling the LLM. It accepts structured outputs. Keep that boundary visible in team integration notes.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Do not treat a seed command as a reset command. Existing orders are left intact. Use separate disposable databases for testing and clean recording fixtures.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Do not report all database behavior as checked when the Postgres variants skipped. Record what environment ran and what remains untested.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Do not infer action success from a button click or an HTTP timeout. Save confirmed outcomes and reconcile uncertain external operations.\par
\pard\s0\f0\fs22\keep\sa120\sl270\slmult0 Do not expand the scope to multiple payment providers, carrier rerouting or multi-tenant accounts until the agreed hackathon path is reliable. Those features require additional data contracts and security boundaries.\par
